{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377356-zanpakuto-and-artifacts-bleach-and-exalted","id":1377356,"title":"Zanpakuto and Artifacts: Bleach and Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-30T09:39:29-07:00","id":1377356,"title":"Zanpakuto and Artifacts: Bleach and Exalted","content":"I've always thought that Exalted's artifact weapons could take a lot from the manga/anime Bleach and how it portrays weapons with integrated spirits. If I were to use the idea fully, here's roughly how I would do it.<br /> <br /> Ratings<br /> <br /> Each artifact weapons would still be rated from 3-5 dots. The artifact's rating would denote the weapon's power ceiling. Before a user started gaining the weapon's evocations, a 3, 4, or 5 dot weapon of the same type would be identical: a blank artifact weapon in terms of stats.<br /> <br /> Once the weapon started gaining evocations, however, the difference would become apparent. 3dot artifacts would gain small permanent evocations and weak active evocations, while a 5 dot would gain large permanent evocations and powerful actives.<br /> <br /> Attunement<br /> <br /> I would change the flat 5 cost attunement to 8-10 or so, modified by the resonant/dissonant factor. A 3 dot resonant artifact would be 5 motes, while a 5 dot resonant would be 15 motes or so. Hideously expensive.<br /> <br /> The reason to make the attunement costs higher is the evocations being 'free' in terms of experience.<br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> <br /> Weapons under this system would gain evocations by milestone or other story reasons, not by buying them. The milestones could be as simple as gaining the weapon's favor by instilling or raising a positive intimacy in the weapon's spirit, or it could be quest related like hunting down and killing the previous wielder or someone/thing the spirit wants dead, protecting someone, etc.<br /> <br /> A weapon would gain evocations that were largely unaffiliated to its current user, meaning each user would gain the same evocations, though there might be differences in order or the bonuses inside some evocations. Maybe some weapons would differ greatly in their evocations between users, but those would be exceptions to the rule.<br /> <br /> Spirits<br /> <br /> Each weapon would have its own spirit, they would be separate from the user, unlike Bleach's method. Each would have its own aims and goals, and some may get along with their users more than others.<br /> <br /> A weapon that changes hands may not be happy that it has a new wielder, and withhold evocations from them until they are won over. Or it might be happy, not having got along with the previous user. The spirit of an abandoned artifact weapon likely will not be happy if it's taken up again by its former wielder.<br /> <br /> Materials and Resonance<br /> <br /> A weapon made from material a user is resonant with will have a cheaper attunement cost, and the weapon's spirit will also get along easier with the user.<br /> <br /> Likewise, a dissonant material will be harder to attune and the spirit less likely to be favorable to the user.<br /> <br /> The relationship between the wielder and the artifact's magical material composition won't override the circumstances of the story regarding the weapon. It will only add another layer of complications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T21:34:42-07:00","id":1377449,"title":"","content":"I think that Bleach is cited in Arms of the Chosen as weapon inspiration, noting that while the story has... Shortcomings, the weapons are pretty neat.<br /> <br /> And y'know what? It's right.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I would probably have Attunement remain where it is, and have the whole kick of Shikai and Bankai be Evocations that require you to commit motes for the duration, and a few bigger Evocations that say &quot;To use this Evocation, [Shikai Evocation] and/or [Bankai Evocation] must be active&quot;<br /> <br /> Example, let's say that we're trying to model Rukia's Zanpakutou. Its base form would be... Actually when sealed, they may take the form of mortal weapons with no powers, to reflect the nature.<br /> <br /> And then it opens up with its first Evocation: <b>Dance, Sode no Shirayuki</b> for 5 motes, which will give it the stats of an Artifact Weapon (Blue Jade, for its icy themes). Then we have a few Evocations that represent the Dances that Rukia demonstrates, which all branch from the first Evocation and all say &quot;This Evocation can only be used when <b>Dance, Sode no Shirayuki</b> is activate&quot;<br /> <br /> Then with training and practice (and maybe building up an Intimacy with the sword's spirit because I do like that idea), Rukia unlocks the next Gate Evocation. <b>Bankai - Hakka no Togame</b>. Probably around... Essence 3? We'll have it cost like 10m, 1wp, and it can only be done when <b>Dance, Sode no Shirayuki</b> is active. Which would bring the total commitment cost for using its powers up to Committing 15m, 1wp.<br /> <br /> ... [Starts making notes]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 03-31-2020, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}